{
  "analysis": "The QEMU monitor socket works and confirms the VM is running. VNC and websockify are listening. However, the HTTP request to `/` returned 502 Bad Gateway, with nginx trying to connect to 127.0.0.1:8080 instead of serving noVNC files. This suggests another nginx config or default proxy is interfering, or the site config wasn't applied as expected. I need to inspect the full nginx configuration and fix the web root serving.",
  "plan": "List nginx config files and inspect the main nginx.conf and enabled sites to find the conflicting proxy to 8080. Then reload/restart nginx after fixing the configuration so port 80 serves noVNC and proxies /websockify to 6080.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/ /etc/nginx/conf.d/; grep -R '8080\\|proxy_pass\\|root\\|listen' /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/ /etc/nginx/conf.d/ /etc/nginx/nginx.conf 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "nginx -T 2>&1 | sed -n '1,160p'\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}
